      <dict>
        <key>boundary</key>
        <string>Two-cut structural prototype only. The lower SC shaft replacement is deliberate and is not labelled whole-body conservation. The four-unit overlap and smooth control field do not prove C1 or raster continuity; actual curve/junction/weight/roles/spacing need review. Independent of held R17 kerning.</string>
        <key>caseSpecificRationale</key>
        <string>Preserve the complete palatal hook, curved foot and deep return.</string>
        <key>construction</key>
        <string>Retain the genuine same-cut SC T crossbar and upper shaft exactly. Intentionally replace the lower shaft below the declared joining band with the complete native lower terminal, including every curl above baseline and every deep palatal-hook curve. Match both actual straight-stem edges across a narrow upper overlap, blending only the straight joining stem above the highest terminal control; every complete terminal curve/counter remains translated unchanged. No clipped-below-baseline fragment, retained square stem stub, generic T alias or capital reduction.</string>
